{"source":"def investigate(context, acquire):
    actions = context.get('actions', [])
    committed = set()
    pending = None
    high = 0
    for action in actions:
        op = action.get('op')
        if op == 'put':
            ident = action.get('id')
            if pending is None:
                committed.add(ident)
            else:
                pending.add(ident)
            if ident > high:
                high = ident
        elif op == 'delete':
            ident = action.get('id')
            if pending is None:
                committed.discard(ident)
            else:
                pending.discard(ident)
        elif op == 'begin':
            pending = set(committed)
        elif op == 'commit':
            committed = set(pending)
            pending = None
        elif op == 'rollback':
            pending = None
            if committed:
                high = max(committed)
    return high + 1
","scope":"Model SQLite INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT allocation: explicit puts raise the durable high-water mark, deletes do not lower it, commits preserve it, and rollback restores the largest ID still present in the committed view (or 0 when empty).","change":"On rollback, discard the pending transactional view and recompute high as max(committed) when committed is nonempty; otherwise leave it unchanged. This fixes rollback cases where an uncommitted larger ID must not advance the next AUTOINCREMENT value while retaining the prior committed maximum."}
